&lt;h1 id=&#34;general-information&#34;&gt;General information
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;shadPS4&lt;/strong&gt; is an early &lt;strong&gt;PlayStation 4&lt;/strong&gt; emulator for &lt;strong&gt;Windows&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Linux&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;macOS&lt;/strong&gt; written in C++.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[!IMPORTANT]
This is the emulator core, which does not include a GUI. If you just want to use the emulator as an end user, download the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadps4-qtlauncher/releases&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;QtLauncher&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; instead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you encounter problems or have doubts, do not hesitate to look at the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4/wiki/I.-Quick-start-%5BUsers%5D&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quickstart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
To verify that a game works, you can look at &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/shadps4-compatibility/shadps4-game-compatibility&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;shadPS4 Game Compatibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
To discuss shadPS4 development, suggest ideas or to ask for help, join our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://discord.gg/bFJxfftGW6&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discord server&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
To get the latest news, go to our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://x.com/shadps4&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;X (Twitter)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; or our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://shadps4.net/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;website&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
You can donate to the project via our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://ko-fi.com/shadps4&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kofi page&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;status&#34;&gt;Status
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[!IMPORTANT]
shadPS4 is early in development, don&amp;rsquo;t expect a flawless experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Currently, the emulator can successfully run games like &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5sZgWyVflFM&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bloodborne&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-3PA-Xwszts&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dark Souls Remastered&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Al7yz_5nLag&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Red Dead Redemption&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, and many other games.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;why&#34;&gt;Why
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;This project began for fun. Given our limited free time, it may take some time before shadPS4 can run more complex games, but we&amp;rsquo;re committed to making small, regular updates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;building&#34;&gt;Building
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;docker&#34;&gt;Docker
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;For building shadPS4 in a containerized environment using Docker and VSCode, check the instructions here:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4/blob/main/documents/building-docker.md&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Docker Build Instructions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;windows&#34;&gt;Windows
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Check the build instructions for &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4/blob/main/documents/building-windows.md&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Windows&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;linux&#34;&gt;Linux
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Check the build instructions for &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4/blob/main/documents/building-linux.md&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Linux&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;macos&#34;&gt;macOS
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Check the build instructions for &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4/blob/main/documents/building-macos.md&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;macOS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[!IMPORTANT]
macOS users need at least macOS 15.4 to run shadPS4. Due to GPU issues there are currently heavy bugs on Intel Macs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;usage-examples&#34;&gt;Usage examples
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[!IMPORTANT]
For a user-friendly GUI, download the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadps4-qtlauncher/releases&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;QtLauncher&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To get the list of all available commands and also a more detailed description of what each command does, please refer to the &lt;code&gt;--help&lt;/code&gt; flag&amp;rsquo;s output.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Below is a list of commonly used command patterns:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;shadPS4 CUSA00001 &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Searches for a game folder called CUSA00001 in the list of game install folders, and boots it.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;shadPS4 --fullscreen &lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; --config-clean CUSA00001    &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# the game argument is always the last one,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;shadPS4 -g CUSA00001 --fullscreen &lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; --config-clean &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# ...unless manually specified otherwise.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;shadPS4 /path/to/game.elf &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Boots a PS4 ELF file directly. Useful if you want to boot an executable that is not named eboot.bin.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;shadPS4 CUSA00001 -- -flag1 -flag2 &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Passes &amp;#39;-flag1&amp;#39; and &amp;#39;-flag2&amp;#39; to the game executable in argv.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1 id=&#34;debugging-and-reporting-issues&#34;&gt;Debugging and reporting issues
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;For more information on how to test, debug and report issues with the emulator or games, read the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4/blob/main/documents/Debugging/Debugging.md&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Debugging documentation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;keyboard-and-mouse-mappings&#34;&gt;Keyboard and Mouse Mappings
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[!NOTE]
Some keyboards may also require you to hold the Fn key to use the F* keys. Mac users should use the Command key instead of Control, and need to use Command+F11 for full screen to avoid conflicting with system key bindings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Button&lt;/th&gt;
