&lt;h1 id=&#34;contributing&#34;&gt;Contributing
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you want to contribute, please read the &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;CONTRIBUTING.md&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; file.&lt;br&gt;
Open a PR and we&amp;rsquo;ll check it :)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;special-thanks&#34;&gt;Special Thanks
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;A few noteworthy teams/projects who&amp;rsquo;ve helped us along the way are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/wheremyfoodat/Panda3DS&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;Panda3DS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: A multiplatform 3DS emulator from our co-author wheremyfoodat. They have been incredibly helpful in understanding and solving problems that came up from natively executing the x64 code of PS4 binaries&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/red-prig/fpPS4&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;fpPS4&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: The fpPS4 team has assisted massively with understanding some of the more complex parts of the PS4 operating system and libraries, by helping with reverse engineering work and research.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;yuzu&lt;/strong&gt;: Our shader compiler has been designed with yuzu&amp;rsquo;s Hades compiler as a blueprint. This allowed us to focus on the challenges of emulating a modern AMD GPU while having a high-quality optimizing shader compiler implementation as a base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/OFFTKP/felix86&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;strong&gt;felix86&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: A new x86-64 → RISC-V Linux userspace emulator&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
